From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yebingiscn <Yebingiscn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] audio/out: keep OHAudio callback nonblocking

Move the potentially blocking OHAudio timestamp IPC to a low-rate clock
thread and publish the result through an atomic snapshot. Use OHAudio's
advanced callback with a nonblocking mpv buffer read, so lock contention
returns zero bytes and lets the audio service back off without consuming
uninitialized data or advancing the device clock with synthetic silence.

Add low-frequency aggregate timing and underrun diagnostics. Healthy windows
remain trace-only; anomalous callback, lock, or clock-query windows emit one
warning line.
---
diff --git a/audio/out/ao_ohaudio.c b/audio/out/ao_ohaudio.c
index 5010eef715..c439cf83fe 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_ohaudio.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_ohaudio.c
@@ -27,36 +27,278 @@
